FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: collation.
OFF THE RECORD: the outstanding fines are collated into ascending
OFF THE RECORD: order by repeated adjacent substitution (a bubble
OFF THE RECORD: sort; the Court prefers procedures that visit
OFF THE RECORD: everything). Schedules are the arrays: 1-indexed,
OFF THE RECORD: read with THE ITEM AT, written with SUBSTITUTE,
OFF THE RECORD: grown with ANNEX.

ARTICLE 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT fines IS A SCHEDULE COMPRISING 500 AND 30 AND 250 AND 30 AND 100.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT n IS THE LENGTH OF fines.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT swapped IS SUSTAINED.

ARTICLE 2.
    SHOULD swapped EQUAL OVERRULED, REFER TO ARTICLE 5.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT swapped IS OVERRULED.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT i IS 1.

ARTICLE 3.
    SHOULD i EXCEED n LESS 1, REFER TO ARTICLE 2.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT a IS THE ITEM AT i IN fines.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT b IS THE ITEM AT i PLUS 1 IN fines.
    SHOULD a EXCEED b, REFER TO ARTICLE 4.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT i IS i PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 3.

ARTICLE 4.
    SUBSTITUTE b FOR ITEM i OF fines.
    SUBSTITUTE a FOR ITEM i PLUS 1 OF fines.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT swapped IS SUSTAINED.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT i IS i PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 3.

ARTICLE 5.
    PROCLAIM fines.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT reading IS AN EMPTY SCHEDULE.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT i IS 1.

ARTICLE 6.
    SHOULD i EXCEED n, REFER TO ARTICLE 7.
    ANNEX THE TRANSCRIPT OF THE ITEM AT i IN fines PLUS " marks" TO reading.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT i IS i PLUS 1.
    REFER TO ARTICLE 6.

ARTICLE 7.
    PROCLAIM THE ITEM AT 1 IN reading.
    PROCLAIM THE LENGTH OF reading.
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
